{
  // TypeScript stage 2, main-process half (BACKLOG 採用#1「残り②」/ Wave0 の
  // 「main checkJs 化」): checkJs over the build-less Electron MAIN-process CJS
  // layer (main.js + ipc-*.js + lib-*.js + preload.js + backup-guard.js).
  //
  // Contract-visibility only — no build, no emit. These files run un-built under
  // Node/Electron, so this project stays checkJs (not .ts). Direct .ts execution
  // waits for Electron 41+ (Node 24 type stripping); until then checkJs beats a
  // hand-written .d.ts that silently drifts from the code. This is the cheap
  // Wave0 win that does NOT need the Electron bump.
  //
  // Separate project from tsconfig.renderer.json because the runtime is Node/CJS,
  // not the DOM/global-IIFE renderer: module is CommonJS, the lib is ES2022 with
  // NO DOM, and only @types/node is auto-included (electron resolves via require).
  //
  // noImplicitAny stays OFF (same rationale as the renderer project): plain JS
  // where internal lambda params would each need JSDoc noise. The rest of strict
  // stays on so real contract breaks (null handling, wrong arg counts to the
  // typed electron/node APIs, missing properties) surface.
  "compilerOptions": {
    "target": "ES2022",
    "lib": ["ES2022"],
    // node16 (not the TS7.0-deprecated "node") — app/package.json has no
    // "type" field, so .js resolves as CommonJS: require/module.exports and
    // extensionless relative requires stay valid.
    "module": "node16",
    "allowJs": true,
    "checkJs": true,
    "noEmit": true,
    "strict": true,
    "noImplicitAny": false,
    // Caught errors stay `any` (pre-4.4 behavior). The main layer reports errors
    // to the renderer via `err.message` at ~9 sites; the renderer service layer
    // never inspects caught errors (it swallows them), so there's no shared
    // narrowing idiom to match. Leaving these as `any` keeps behavior byte-
    // identical instead of forcing `instanceof Error` guards that would change
    // the non-Error error string. Same "don't model internal idiom noise" spirit
    // as noImplicitAny above; the rest of strict stays on.
    "useUnknownInCatchVariables": false,
    "forceConsistentCasingInFileNames": true,
    "skipLibCheck": true,
    "types": ["node"]
  },
  "files": ["main.js", "preload.js", "backup-guard.js", "ipc-backup.js", "ipc-config.js", "ipc-organize.js", "ipc-posts.js", "ipc-transfer.js", "ipc-trash.js", "ipc-window.js", "lib-archive.js", "lib-imgsize.js", "lib-index.js", "lib-json.js", "lib-migrate.js"]
}
